"/>\n<path d=\"M1.73071 2.24432H16.3691\" stroke=\"var(--meadow-accent-color)\" stroke-width=\"2.14929\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M1.73071 13.6622H7.77047\" stroke=\"var(--meadow-accent-color)\" stroke-width=\"2.14929\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n</svg>\n</span> Notes</a></div>\n  <div class=\"wprm-layout-column-container wprm-column-gap-40 wprm-column-rows-recipe-900 meadow-main-columns\">\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-left\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-8415-ingredients\" class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients-container wprm-recipe-8415-ingredients-container wprm-block-text-normal wprm-ingredient-style-regular wprm-recipe-images-before\" data-recipe=\"8415\" data-servings=\"10\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-ingredients-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Ingredients<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-ingredients wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">10</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">pieces</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">frozen egg rolls</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">ready for cooking</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"2\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cups</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">vegetable oil</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for frying</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"3\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">optional dipping sauce</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">sweet chili sauce or soy sauce</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-8415-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"8415\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">2 cups vegetable oil&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">for frying</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 deep skillet or saucepan&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">for frying the egg rolls</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-8415-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-8415-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"8415\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8415-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Heat the Oil &#8211; Heat vegetable oil in a deep skillet or saucepan over medium-high heat until it reaches 350°F (175°C).</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8415-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Fry the Egg Rolls &#8211; Carefully place frozen egg rolls into the hot oil, making sure not to overcrowd the pan.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8415-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Cook Until Golden &#8211; Fry for 4–6 minutes, turning occasionally, until golden brown and crispy.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8415-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Drain the Egg Rolls &#8211; Remove egg rolls with a slotted spoon and drain on paper towels.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8415-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Serve and Enjoy! &#8211; Serve hot with your favorite dipping sauce.</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-8415-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>200</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>10g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>5g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>25g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these simple ingredients to make delicious frozen <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egg_roll\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">egg rolls</a>!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Crispy-Frozen-Egg-Rolls-Ready-for-Frying.webp\" alt=\"A plate of golden-brown frozen egg rolls with dipping sauces on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-8413\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Crispy-Frozen-Egg-Rolls-Ready-for-Frying.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Crispy-Frozen-Egg-Rolls-Ready-for-Frying-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>10 frozen egg rolls</strong> – ready for cooking</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 cups vegetable oil</strong> – for frying</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>optional dipping sauce</strong> – sweet chili sauce or soy sauce</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-frozen-egg-rolls\"><strong>How to Make frozen egg rolls</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Making frozen egg rolls is a breeze! With a preparation time of just 5 minutes and a cooking time of 4–6 minutes, you’ll have a delicious appetizer ready in no time. If you want to let them rest for a minute after frying, that’s just a little extra time to ensure they’re perfectly crispy!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Frying-Frozen-Egg-Rolls.webp\" alt=\"Four-step process of frying frozen egg rolls, showing heating oil, placing egg rolls in oil, frying until golden, and draining on paper towels.\" class=\"wp-image-8414\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Frying-Frozen-Egg-Rolls.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Frying-Frozen-Egg-Rolls-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Heat the Oil</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Heat vegetable oil in a deep skillet or saucepan over medium-high heat until it reaches 350°F (175°C).</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Fry the Egg Rolls</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Carefully place frozen egg rolls into the hot oil, making sure not to overcrowd the pan.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Cook Until Golden</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Fry for 4–6 minutes, turning occasionally, until golden brown and crispy.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Drain the Egg Rolls</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Remove egg rolls with a slotted spoon and drain on paper towels.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Serve and Enjoy!</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Serve hot with your favorite dipping sauce.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Appetizer / Snack</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>Asian</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>5 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>6 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>1 minute resting</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>12 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Hot with dipping sauce</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-frozen-egg-rolls\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making frozen egg rolls</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw your egg rolls in the fridge overnight for even cooking.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Brush with a little oil before baking for extra crispiness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with fillings like veggies or chicken for variety.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Don’t overcrowd the baking sheet to ensure even heat distribution.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with a homemade dipping sauce for a personal touch.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-frozen-egg-rolls\"><strong>How to Serve this frozen egg rolls</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve with sweet and sour sauce for a tangy dip.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with soy sauce or teriyaki sauce for an umami kick.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy alongside a fresh cucumber salad for a crunchy contrast.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Offer a side of spicy chili sauce for those who love heat.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Garnish with chopped green onions for a pop of color.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve on a platter with a variety of dipping sauces for a fun appetizer spread.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s how to keep your frozen egg rolls fresh and delicious:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow egg rolls to cool completely.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place in an airtight container or wrap tightly in plastic wrap.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Cool cooked egg rolls completely before freezing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Arrange in a single layer on a baking sheet.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Freeze until solid, then transfer to a freezer bag.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label and date the bag; use within 2-3 months for best quality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>For best results, reheat in the oven at 375°F (190°C) for 15-20 minutes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Alternatively, use an air fryer for 10-12 minutes at 350°F (175°C).</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Microwave for a quick option, but expect a softer texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Always check that they are heated through before serving.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What is the best frozen egg roll to buy?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>When looking for the best frozen egg rolls, consider brands that prioritize quality ingredients and authentic flavors. Popular choices include Tai Pei and Pagoda, which offer a variety of fillings and are known for their crispy texture. Always check the ingredient list for natural ingredients and avoid those with artificial additives for a healthier option.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What is the best way to cook frozen egg rolls?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The best way to cook frozen egg rolls is to bake them in the oven for a crispy texture. Preheat your oven to 400°F (200°C), place the egg rolls on a baking sheet, and bake for about 15-20 minutes, turning halfway through. Alternatively, you can air fry them for about 10-12 minutes at the same temperature for an even crispier result. Avoid microwaving, as this can make them soggy.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. Which frozen spring rolls are best?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>For frozen spring rolls, brands like Spring Home and Ling Ling are often recommended for their authentic taste and quality. Look for options that feature a variety of fillings, such as vegetable or shrimp, and check for a crispy texture upon cooking. Reading reviews can also help you find the best options available in your area.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. Are pagoda egg rolls any good?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Pagoda egg rolls are generally well-received for their flavor and crunch. They offer a variety of fillings, including chicken and vegetable options, making them a versatile choice for appetizers. Many people enjoy their taste and texture, especially when cooked according to the package instructions for optimal crispiness.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Now that you have this delightful frozen egg rolls recipe in your back pocket, it’s time to get cooking! These crispy bites are not just easy to make, but they also bring a taste of nostalgia to your table. Enjoy them with your favorite dipping sauce and share the joy with friends and family. Happy cooking!</p>\n",
